# Trivy deploy-gate suppressions (read automatically by the trivy-action in
# deploy.yml — "Trivy gate (CRITICAL,HIGH; fail closed)").
#
# Each entry is a DOCUMENTED, time-boxed risk-acceptance, not a "fix". Remove the
# entry as soon as the underlying dependency can be patched.
#
# ── multer 2.1.1 Denial-of-Service advisories ───────────────────────────────
# The patch is multer 2.2.0, but @nestjs/platform-express pins multer EXACTLY
# 2.1.1 (even in its latest release, 11.1.27) and npm 11.9.0 silently refuses to
# apply an `overrides` bump, so the version cannot be raised cleanly yet.
#
# Risk is mitigated and LOW in context:
#   - the only code paths that reach multer are the image-upload endpoints,
#   - which are AUTH-GATED (vendor/admin only),
#   - RATE-LIMITED (RATE_LIMIT_CALLBACK, 20/min/IP) behind Cloudflare,
#   - fileSize-capped (10 MB), and
#   - fields/parts/fieldNameSize-capped (PR #385) — which closes the
#     "deeply nested field names" DoS vector at the app layer.
#
# REMOVE these once NestJS ships a @nestjs/platform-express that depends on a
# patched multer (Dependabot will open that PR). Tracked in the project memory
# note `reference_deploy_trivy_gate`.
CVE-2026-5079
GHSA-72gw-mp4g-v24j
GHSA-3p4h-7m6x-2hcm

# ── deepmerge-ts 7.1.5 — CVE-2026-40345 (stack exhaustion) ─────────────────
# Review by: 2026-09-30
#
# Newly published advisory; nothing in this repo changed to introduce it.
# Reached only as prisma -> @prisma/config -> deepmerge-ts. The fix is
# deepmerge-ts 8.0.0, but @prisma/config pins 7.1.5 exactly and npm refuses a
# root `overrides` bump against an exact pin (verified: the override leaves
# 7.1.5 in the tree). No published prisma release ships a patched copy, so
# there is nothing to upgrade to.
#
# Risk is LOW in context: the advisory is stack exhaustion when merging
# deeply-recursive objects. @prisma/config uses deepmerge-ts to merge OUR OWN
# prisma config at CLI/build time — it never merges request data, and no
# runtime request path reaches it. An attacker would need write access to the
# repo's prisma config, at which point this CVE is irrelevant.
#
# Already waived for the npm gate as GHSA-ggr8-5vv4-36mx in
# .audit-allowlist.json; this is the same advisory under its CVE id, which is
# what Trivy matches on. Remove BOTH together when prisma ships a fix.
CVE-2026-40345
